The fence flow is the executable product contract: one authenticated request is admitted by Quality, authorized by Guard, durably handed off by Bus, and completed with tamper-evident audit evidence. text Copy POST /v1/fence/submit
   │
   ├── Quality admission ── fail ─▶ blocked_by_quality
   │        │ pass
   ├── Guard enforcement ── deny ─▶ blocked_by_guard
   │        │ allow
   ├── durable Bus handoff ─ fail ─▶ unavailable / configured advisory outcome
   │        │ committed
   └── fence.completed audit ──────▶ handed_off # Outcomes final_outcome allowed Meaning handed_off true Admission passed, Guard allowed, durable handoff and completion audit succeeded blocked_by_quality false Admission rejected the artifact blocked_by_guard false Guard denied/held the action authorized_not_delivered true Only possible where Bus is explicitly advisory; authorization did not become a false delivery claim # Receipt The receipt carries one correlation identity across the three stages and audit trail. json Copy {
  "request_id": "req_…",
  "allowed": true,
  "final_outcome": "handed_off",
  "stages": {
    "quality": {"mode":"admission","profile":"default","passed":true},
    "guard": {"outcome":"allow","reason_codes":["GUARD_ALLOW"],"matched_rule":"baseline:read-only-low-risk"},
    "bus": {"delivered":true,"workspace":"tenant:…","message_id":"M…"}
  },
  "audit": {"event_id":"…","sequence":42,"event_hash":"…","signing_key_id":"…"}
} # Resilience Guard is always fail closed. Quality and Bus are fail closed by default and may only be made advisory deliberately. Database, signing requirements and completion-audit persistence fail closed. Optional telemetry/broker fan-out may degrade without changing an authorization decision. Read the complete failure contract → # Direct Guard vs full fence Endpoint Use when POST /guard/v1/decisions You need an enforcement decision only POST /v1/fence/submit You need Quality → Guard → durable Bus → audit as one governed transaction
